4.Create a VIEW named TopSpendersView that shows usernames and order_total from a FoodOrder table where order_total is greater than 1000.
Ans.
create view TopSpendersView AS
select username,order_total
from SpotifyUser
join FoodOrder
on SpotifyUser.user_id=FoodOrder.user_id
where FoodOrder.order_total>1000;


5.Write a SQL query to list all users from the TopSpendersView who have spent more than 2000, sorted by order_total descending.<br><br><em><strong>Constraint:</strong> Only use the TopSpendersView for your query, not the original FoodOrder table.</em> with output
Ans.
select username, order_total
from TopSpendersView
where order_total>2000
order by order_total desc
